# Does the game stay correct while the freeing thread's Sleep is capped (mcla_pump_sleep_max_ms)? (cpu-profile work)
# Run it WITHOUT --mcla_fixed_dt (real-time steps) and with --mcla_fps=0 (uncapped). Boot -> title -> city, then a drive
# whose steps are in wall time (cpup-roam.pad's are engine frames, so the car would leave the car park at another speed
# at another frame rate), sampled every 2 s by cpup-sample.pad (wall clock, engine frames, swaps, the freeing thread's
# rounds, the game clock, the position): at a correct game the game clock advances one second a second, the car covers
# the same ground in the same time whatever the frame rate, and the engine frames and swaps are what the frame rate is.
# Then the frame-rate caps 120, 60 and 30 are set with `set mcla_fps` while the car coasts to a stop, 8 s each: the swaps
# a second must be the cap, whatever the thread's Sleep. Marks: title, map_zoom, free_roam, roam, drive, cap120, cap60,
# cap30, end.
wait 8s
mark title
press_until start left_title every=2s timeout=90s
mark map_zoom
wait_until roam 180s
mark free_roam
wait 8s
mark roam
include cpup-sample.pad
trigger rt 1 0.35s
trigger rt 0.6
stick lx 1 0.28s
trigger rt 1
mark drive
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 2s
include cpup-sample.pad
release all
set mcla_fps 120
mark cap120
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 8s
include cpup-sample.pad
set mcla_fps 60
mark cap60
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 8s
include cpup-sample.pad
set mcla_fps 30
mark cap30
include cpup-sample.pad
wait 8s
include cpup-sample.pad
set mcla_fps 0
mark end
